From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fix <fix@fix.fix>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmtk: Reset MT7925 before firmware download

After a warm reboot the MT7925 BT core can retain its pre-reboot
firmware state. The WMT bulk-transfer path becomes unresponsive while
UHW register access (vendor control requests) still works. This causes
the initial PATCH_DWNLD WMT command in btmtk_setup_firmware_79xx() to
time out (-ETIMEDOUT).

Call btmtk_usb_subsys_reset() for MT7925 before firmware download to
return the chip to ROM state, making it ready to receive firmware
regardless of reboot type.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
@@ -1326,6 +1326,14 @@ int btmtk_usb_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 	case 0x7922:
 	case 0x7925:
 	case 0x7961:
+		if (dev_id == 0x7925) {
+			err = btmtk_usb_subsys_reset(hdev, dev_id);
+			if (err < 0) {
+				bt_dev_err(hdev, "Subsystem reset failed (%d)", err);
+				return err;
+			}
+		}
+
 		btmtk_fw_get_filename(fw_bin_name, sizeof(fw_bin_name), dev_id,
 				      fw_version, fw_flavor);

